      ],
      "source": "https://www.stowehistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The society’s archives live in two one‑room schoolhouses on School Street beside the Waterbury River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stowehistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stowe lies between Pottstown to the east and Berks County to the west, with the Schuylkill River marking its southern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stowe%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Grosstown Road, the main north‑south artery, meets Route 422 at its southern terminus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stowe%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Stowe sits in hardiness zone 7a, where the climate borders humid subtropical and hot‑summer humid continental.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
